# Stubbed symbols that ADI is known to call, and that are known to be harmless.
#
# These are the difference between an alarm worth reading and one people learn to ignore.
# Anything in this file logs at INFO and is not counted as a reason to distrust the session;
# anything NOT in this file logs at ERROR, because it means Apple's implementation started
# depending on something we only pretend to provide.
#
# Add to this list only with evidence - a passing end-to-end provisioning run with the call
# observed - never because a log line was annoying.

# Called from a static constructor while dlopen'ing libstoreservicescore.so, before any ADI
# function runs. Our stub returns NULL.
#
# Harmless, established two ways. Provisioning completes successfully with the NULL: verified
# by AdiProvisioningTest against Apple's real servers on 2026-08-10 (session completed,
# ADIGetLoginCode then returned 0). And the reference implementation is in the same position
# by construction - Dadoum/Provision's loader never runs .init_array at all, so this
# constructor does not execute there either, and every public Anisette server runs that way.
F _ZN13mediaplatform9WorkQueue13makeWorkQueueERKNSt6__ndk112basic_stringIcNS1_11char_traitsIcEENS1_9allocatorIcEEEENS0_13WorkQueueTypeE
